Category: Knowledge Versioning
Purpose:
  Defines knowledge versioning with history preservation,
  change tracking, rollback procedures, and promotion rules.
  Ensures every knowledge change is traceable and reversible.

Owns: ./

Versioning Schema:

  Every knowledge element has a version field:

    @skill.repository
      v: 1
      definition: repository owns persistence
      changed_reason: initial definition
      changed_at: <timestamp>
      changed_by: <agent/human>

  On change, version increments:

    v1:
      definition: repository owns persistence
      changed_reason: initial definition

    v2:
      definition: repository owns persistence, but domain policy remains outside
      changed_reason: observed 4 production cases requiring policy separation

Versioning Rules:
  [V1] Every change MUST increment the version number.
  [V2] Every version MUST have a changed_reason field.
  [V3] Every version MUST record changed_at timestamp.
  [V4] Every version MUST record changed_by (agent or human).
  [V5] Previous versions are preserved — never overwritten.
  [V6] The latest active version is the default reference target.

Change Tracking:

  changed_reason MUST reference evidence:
    - @project.<name>      — which project triggered the change
    - @review.<id>         — which review identified the need
    - @decision.<id>       — which decision mandated the change
    - @observation.<type>  — what was observed in code/production

  Example:
    changed_reason:
      observed: 4 production cases of policy leakage
      decision: @decision.088
      project: @project.payment

Rollback Procedure:

  Trigger: regression detected in production from new knowledge pattern.

  Steps:
    1. Identify problematic version (e.g., v3).
    2. Mark status: deprecated.
    3. Revert to last known stable version (e.g., v2).
    4. Record rollback reason and evidence.
    5. Create candidate for alternative approach.

  State transitions:
    v3 (active) → v3 (deprecated) → v2 (active)

  Example:
    @skill.new-pattern
      v: 3
      status: deprecated
      rollback_to: v2
      rollback_reason: production incident INC-2041

Version Promotion Rules:

  Knowledge progresses through trust levels:

    CANDIDATE     — newly observed, unvalidated
    VALIDATED      — confirmed by evidence or human review
    ESTABLISHED    — proven across multiple projects/tasks
    DEPRECATED     — superseded or disproven

  Promotion conditions:
    CANDIDATE → VALIDATED:    evidence from ≥1 project + human review
    VALIDATED → ESTABLISHED:  evidence from ≥3 projects or ≥5 tasks
    ANY → DEPRECATED:         contradicted by evidence or replaced

  [P1] AI MUST NOT promote knowledge without meeting evidence thresholds.
  [P2] Human can manually promote/demote at any time.
  [P3] Promoted knowledge inherits version history.
  [P4] Deprecated knowledge remains visible with status label.

